<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aditya I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">reigned c. 871–907</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Aditya Chola I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aditya I was king of the Chola dynasty of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in the late 9th century, the son of Vijayalaya. Around 897 he defeated the Pallava king Aparajita, annexed the Pallava lands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tondaimandalam">Tondaimandalam</a> and made the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Cholas</a> the leading power in the Tamil country. He was a great builder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiva">Shiva</a> temples, and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parantaka-i">Parantaka I</a> extended Chola rule further south.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aditya-i.jpg" alt="Aditya I" width="320" height="228" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Venu62 (talk) (Uploads) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aditya_territories.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
